---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Trainer Mentorship &amp; Workshops | Bransky Fitness"
  description="One-on-one mentorship and workshops for personal trainers, led by Mark Bransky, NASM Master Trainer with nearly 20 years of experience and 1,500+ trainers certified."
  path="/trainer-development/"
  activeNav="trainer-development"
>

  <section class="page-intro facets">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h1>Personal Trainer Mentorship</h1>
      <p>Simple systems. Tailored feedback. Master your craft.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-label="Mentorship overview">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 46rem;">
      <p style="font-size:1.1rem;">Mentorship for serious trainers who love training and want structured support, accountability, and real-world feedback to master coaching and build a sustainable business.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-dark facets-dark" aria-labelledby="story-heading">
    <div class="wrap" style="max-width: 46rem;">
      <p class="eyebrow" style="font-weight:600; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">My story</p>
      <h2 id="story-heading">Twenty years and 20,000+ sessions later</h2>
      <p>Those first months nearly broke me. Every client interaction felt like a test I wasn't prepared for. Every assessment was a guessing game. Every program I wrote felt like throwing darts in the dark, hoping something would stick. The imposter syndrome was suffocating.</p>
      <p>But here's what I discovered: every master trainer has felt exactly this way. The difference isn't talent, it's having the right guide at the right time. I found mentors who transformed my anxiety into expertise. Twenty years and 20,000+ sessions later, I've made it my mission to be that guide for trainers who are exactly where I was: talented, driven, but desperately needing someone to show them the way.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="help-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="help-heading">How I can help</h2>
        <p class="lede">Four areas mentees work on most, depending on where you are in your career.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="program-grid">
        <div class="program-card">
          <h3>NASM prep &amp; study guidance</h3>
          <p>Master the material and pass your certification with confidence.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="program-card">
          <h3>Client assessments &amp; program troubleshooting</h3>
          <p>Learn to identify movement issues and create programs that actually work.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="program-card">
          <h3>Exercise technique &amp; coaching skills</h3>
          <p>Develop the cueing and correction skills that separate pros from amateurs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="program-card">
          <h3>Career strategy &amp; business development</h3>
          <p>Build a thriving practice that attracts quality clients and premium rates.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="facets" aria-labelledby="works-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="works-heading">Here's how it works</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="method-list" style="max-width:44rem; margin-inline:auto;">
        <li class="method-item">
          <span class="method-step">1</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Discovery session</h3>
            <p>We schedule your session and you complete a detailed questionnaire so I can learn about you, your business, and your specific goals before we meet.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="method-item">
          <span class="method-step">2</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Mentorship</h3>
            <p>We meet for one hour, in person or virtual, to discuss your goals, create a personalized roadmap for success, and work on the specific skills, knowledge, and resources you need to achieve them.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li class="method-item">
          <span class="method-step">3</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Follow-up &amp; refine</h3>
            <p>I follow up with a 15-minute phone call to see how well your plan is working and help you make any necessary adjustments to ensure you're on track for success.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="mentor-testimonials-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <h2 id="mentor-testimonials-heading">Achieve more, grow faster, be more confident</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="testimonial-grid compact" style="border-top:none; padding-top:0; margin-top:0;">
        <blockquote class="testimonial">
          <p>"Mark helped me communicate complex ideas with more clarity and confidence. His precise, down-to-earth teaching style made everything click, and made learning fun."</p>
          <cite>Peter Dowd, Equinox Tier X, Master Kettlebell Instructor</cite>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="testimonial">
          <p>"Mark's assessments and corrective strategies gave me clarity and confidence in my programming. He helped connect the dots between textbook learning and real-world coaching."</p>
          <cite>Adam Turrey, Lucid Motion Fitness</cite>
        </blockquote>
        <blockquote class="testimonial">
          <p>"Mark helped me refine my programming decisions and build real confidence in applying assessments. His supportive, non-judgmental coaching made it easy to ask questions and grow through curiosity."</p>
          <cite>Carolina R.</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-dark facets-dark" aria-labelledby="mentor-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <figure class="about-figure">
          <img src="/images/mentor-group.jpg" alt="Mark Bransky with a cohort of personal trainers he mentored" width="1040" height="628" loading="lazy">
        </figure>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow" style="font-weight:600; margin-bottom:0.5rem;">Meet your mentor</p>
          <h2 id="mentor-heading">Mark Bransky, M.S., NASM Master Trainer</h2>
          <p>With nearly 20 years in the industry, 20,000+ sessions serviced, and 1,500+ trainers certified, I've seen it all. But more importantly, I've taught it all.</p>
          <ul class="credential-list">
            <li>Master's in Exercise Science &amp; Health Promotion</li>
            <li>NASM Master Trainer</li>
            <li>Certified Personal Trainer (CPT)</li>
            <li>Corrective Exercise Specialization (CES)</li>
            <li>Performance Enhancement Specialist (PES)</li>
            <li>Youth Exercise Specialization (YES)</li>
            <li>Senior Fitness Specialization (SFS)</li>
            <li>Weight Loss Specialist (WLS)</li>
            <li>Certified Nutrition Coach (CNC)</li>
            <li>Golf Fitness Specialization (GFS)</li>
            <li>Behavior Change Specialization (BCS)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="workshops-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="about-grid">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow-light">Workshops</p>
          <h2 id="workshops-heading">Elevate your training</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--ink-soft); font-style:italic;">You assess and program by feel. Your clients see results, then plateau. You're not sure what changed.</p>
          <p>Master a system, so you know exactly what you're assessing, program with confidence, and actually keep clients long-term. Whether you're building your solo practice, working in a larger facility, or scaling a coaching business, my workshops give you a simple, repeatable process to identify movement limitations, guide individualized programming, and become the trainer clients don't want to leave.</p>
          <p><strong>Why trainers choose this:</strong> As a NASM Master Trainer and certified CPR instructor, I've worked with thousands of trainers across the country. The ones who stand out aren't the ones with the most clients. They're the ones who can confidently explain why they assessed what they did and why they programmed it that way.</p>
          <p><strong>What you get:</strong> Not another certification. A framework you actually use, every session, that makes you sharper and more credible with every client.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="about-figure">
          <img src="/images/mentor-bw.jpg" alt="Mark Bransky coaching a trainer through a loaded lunge in a workshop setting" width="640" height="522" loading="lazy">
        </figure>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-band" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 id="cta-heading">Ready to get started?</h2>
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/contact/">Let's Go!</a>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
